    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0480" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to
                        President Roosevelt</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>, [<date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-16">September 16, 1944</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>. I return the Memorandum you gave
                    me about Italian Colonies.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d243-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Foreign Office would like to treat this as an official communication if you
                    would allow us to keep a copy of it.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d243-f2"/></p>
                <p>It seems that the usual broad and substantial measure of agreement exists between
                    us, but we should like to look into the details more closely.</p>
                <closer><signed>W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">inston</hi>] S C[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hurchill</hi>]</signed><lb/>16.9.44.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d243-f1" n="1" xml:id="d243-f1-content">
                <p>The paper attached to this communication is the ribbon copy of Hull’s memorandum
                    to Roosevelt of September 11, 1944, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg408">p. 408</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d243-f2" n="2" xml:id="d243-f2-content">
                <p>Attnched to this memorandum in the Roosevelt Papers is the following handwritten
                    note: “The President told the P. M. OK to keep
                    copies of attached &amp; he also said he wanted an answer from the British on
                    it. D[<hi rendition="#small-caps">orothy</hi>] J B[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >rady</hi>].”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
